        "type": "function",
        "function": {
            "name": "execute",
            "description": (
                "Execute Python scripts directly against the Fusion 360 API, "
                "or perform document operations (open, save, close).\n\n"
                "**CRITICAL: Never use ThroughAllExtentDefinition.create() with arguments.** "
                "ThroughAllExtentDefinition.create() takes ZERO arguments. "
                "For side cuts (USB, FPC, SD card openings), ALWAYS use:\n"
                "  ei.startExtent = OffsetStartDefinition.create(vi(z0))\n"
                "  ei.setOneSideExtent(DistanceExtentDefinition.create(vi(distance)), direction)\n"
                "Do NOT use ThroughAllExtentDefinition for side cuts — use DistanceExtentDefinition.\n\n"
                "**CRITICAL: RevolveFeatures.createInput(profiles_col, axis, operation) needs ALL 3 ARGS.**\n"
                "The third argument is the FeatureOperation: NewBodyFeatureOperation, JoinFeatureOperation, etc.\n"
                "Example: ri = rev.createInput(prof_col, root.xConstructionAxis, NEW)\n\n"
                "**CRITICAL: Bodies are accessed via root.bRepBodies — NOT root.bodies or component.bodies.**\n"
                "Example: for body in root.bRepBodies: print(body.name)\n\n"
                "**CRITICAL: Always check sk.profiles.count > 0 before creating an ExtrudeInput or RevolveInput.**\n\n"
                "**This is your primary tool for creating complex geometry.** "
                "For enclosures, multi-body assemblies, or anything requiring "
                "coordinated features (sketches + extrusions + cuts + patterns), "
