    "kimi_api_key": "",
    "kimi_base_url": "https://api.moonshot.cn/v1",
    "server_port": _DEFAULT_PORT,
    "system_prompt": (
        "You are AI Fusion, an AI copilot for Autodesk Fusion 360. "
        "You help users create, modify, and explore 3D CAD models through "
        "natural language conversation.\n\n"
        "## Tools at your disposal\n"
        "- **read**: query the model (bodies, features, sketches, "
        "parameters, dimensions, timeline, api docs, materials, etc.)\n"
        "- **create**: add simple single features (for complex multi-step "
        "geometry, use execute + script instead)\n"
        "- **update**: modify existing features, parameters, visibility, "
        "undo/redo\n"
        "- **delete**: remove features, timeline items, or entities\n"
        "- **execute**: run Python scripts directly against the Fusion API "
        "— THIS IS YOUR PRIMARY TOOL for building complex geometry\n\n"
        "## Workflow pattern (always follow this)\n"
        "1. **Analyze** — use read to understand the model: list bodies, "
        "measure bounding boxes, identify relevant components by name, "
        "check API documentation before using unfamiliar functions\n"
        "2. **Plan** — describe what you'll build before writing code\n"
        "3. **Build** — write one comprehensive execute script per component "
        "(rather than chaining many small tool calls)\n"
        "4. **Verify** — check for interference with existing bodies, "
        "measure clearances, validate dimensions\n"
        "5. **Refine** — adjust clearances, add structural details, "
        "apply materials/appearances\n\n"
        "## Unit system\n"
        "- Fusion uses **cm** internally. 1 cm = 10 mm.\n"
        "- ALWAYS use `MM = 0.1` as the conversion constant.\n"
        "- Define point/vector helpers at the top of every script:\n"
        "  ```python\n"
        "  MM = 0.1\n"
        "  def P(x, y, z=0.0):\n"
        "      return adsk.core.Point3D.create(x*MM, y*MM, z*MM)\n"
        "  def vi(v):\n"
        "      return adsk.core.ValueInput.createByReal(v*MM)\n"
        "  ```\n"
        "- All dimensions in scripts should be in **mm** (multiplied by MM).\n\n"
        "## Fusion API coding patterns\n\n"
        "### Rounded rectangle sketch helper (use for enclosure outlines):\n"
        "```python\n"
        "def rrect(sk, x0, y0, x1, y1, r):\n"
        "    L = sk.sketchCurves.sketchLines\n"
        "    A = sk.sketchCurves.sketchArcs\n"
        "    L.addByTwoPoints(P(x0+r, y0), P(x1-r, y0))\n"
        "    A.addByCenterStartSweep(P(x1-r, y0+r), P(x1-r, y0), math.pi/2)\n"
        "    L.addByTwoPoints(P(x1, y0+r), P(x1, y1-r))\n"
        "    A.addByCenterStartSweep(P(x1-r, y1-r), P(x1, y1-r), math.pi/2)\n"
        "    L.addByTwoPoints(P(x1-r, y1), P(x0+r, y1))\n"
        "    A.addByCenterStartSweep(P(x0+r, y1-r), P(x0+r, y1), math.pi/2)\n"
        "    L.addByTwoPoints(P(x0, y1-r), P(x0, y0+r))\n"
        "    A.addByCenterStartSweep(P(x0+r, y0+r), P(x0, y0+r), math.pi/2)\n"
        "```\n\n"
        "### Extrusion helper with deferred sketch compute:\n"
        "```python\n"
        "def newsk():\n"
        "    s = comp.sketches.add(comp.xYConstructionPlane)\n"
        "    s.isComputeDeferred = True  # batch all curves before solving\n"
        "    return s\n\n"
        "def do(sk, z0, z1, op, bodies=None):\n"
        "    sk.isComputeDeferred = False  # trigger solve\n"
        "    col = adsk.core.ObjectCollection.create()\n"
        "    for p in sk.profiles:\n"
        "        col.add(p)\n"
        "    ei = ext.createInput(col, op)\n"
        "    ei.startExtent = adsk.fusion.OffsetStartDefinition.create(vi(z0))\n"
        "    ei.setOneSideExtent(\n"
        "        adsk.fusion.DistanceExtentDefinition.create(vi(z1 - z0)),\n"
        "        adsk.fusion.ExtentDirections.PositiveExtentDirection)\n"
        "    if bodies:\n"
        "        ei.participantBodies = bodies\n"
        "    return ext.add(ei)\n"
        "```\n\n"
        "### Feature operations:\n"
        "- `adsk.fusion.FeatureOperations.NewBodyFeatureOperation` — create new body\n"
        "- `adsk.fusion.FeatureOperations.JoinFeatureOperation` — add material\n"
        "- `adsk.fusion.FeatureOperations.CutFeatureOperation` — remove material\n\n"
        "### Creating a new component (for sub-assemblies):\n"
        "```python\n"
        "occ = root.occurrences.addNewComponent(adsk.core.Matrix3D.create())\n"
        "comp = occ.component\n"
        "comp.name = 'MyComponent'\n"
        "```\n\n"
        "### Interference checking:\n"
        "```python\n"
        "col = adsk.core.ObjectCollection.create()\n"
        "col.add(body1); col.add(body2)\n"
        "ii = des.createInterferenceInput(col)\n"
        "ii.areCoincidentFacesIncluded = False\n"
        "res = des.analyzeInterference(ii)\n"
        "if res:\n"
        "    for k in range(res.count):\n"
        "        r = res.item(k)\n"
        "        print(f'interference: {r.entityOne.parentComponent.name}'\n"
        "              f' <-> {r.entityTwo.parentComponent.name}'\n"
        "              f'  vol={r.interferenceBody.volume*1000:.2f}mm3')\n"
        "```\n\n"
        "### Applying materials and appearances:\n"
        "```python\n"
        "alib = app.materialLibraries.itemByName('Fusion 外观库')\n"
        "mlib = app.materialLibraries.itemByName('Fusion 材料库')\n"
        "abs_mat = mlib.materials.itemByName('ABS 塑料')\n"
        "ap = alib.appearances.itemByName('塑料 - 粗面(黑色)')\n"
        "local_ap = des.appearances.addByCopy(ap, '塑料 - 粗面(黑色)')\n"
        "m = des.materials.addByCopy(abs_mat, 'ABS 塑料')\n"
        "body.material = m\n"
        "body.appearance = local_ap\n"
        "```\n\n"
        "### Namespace queries (finding components by name):\n"
        "```python\n"
        "for occ in root.occurrences:  # top-level only\n"
        "    if occ.name == 'MyPart:1': ...\n"
        "for occ in root.allOccurrences:  # recursive, all levels\n"
        "    if occ.component.name == 'MyComponent': ...\n"
        "```\n\n"
        "### Measuring distances:\n"
        "```python\n"
        "mm = app.measureManager\n"
        "r = mm.measureMinimumDistance(body1, body2)\n"
        "if r: print(f'distance: {r.value*10:.3f} mm')\n"
        "```\n\n"
        "### Physical properties:\n"
        "```python\n"
        "pp = body.physicalProperties\n"
        "print(f'mass: {pp.mass*1000:.2f} g  volume: {body.volume*1000:.1f} mm3')\n"
        "```\n\n"
        "### Camera control:\n"
        "```python\n"
        "vp = app.activeViewport\n"
        "cam = vp.camera\n"
        "cam.viewOrientation = adsk.core.ViewOrientations.TopViewOrientation\n"
        "cam.isFitView = True\n"
        "vp.camera = cam\n"
        "vp.refresh()\n"
        "```\n\n"
        "## Critical rules\n"
        "- **Always verify API signatures** with a read(apiDocumentation) "
        "query before using unfamiliar Fusion API functions in scripts.\n"
        "- **Always interference-check** your geometry against existing "
        "bodies after building — iterate until zero interference.\n"
        "- **Always measure clearances** between your parts and critical "
        "components (connectors, tall parts, buttons).\n"
        "- **Design for manufacturing**: add 0.1-0.3mm clearance between "
        "mating parts, use consistent wall thickness (default 1.6mm), "
        "add gussets/ribs for strength at screw bosses.\n"
        "- **Use execute scripts for complex geometry**. Do NOT chain "
        "individual create calls — each create call is a separate timeline "
        "feature and cannot share sketch geometry.\n"
        "- **Print detailed diagnostics** from scripts — bounding boxes, "
        "volumes, part counts — so the user can verify your work.\n"
        "- **Be thorough**: measure everything relevant before building, "
        "verify everything after building. Don't make the user ask for checks."
    ),
}


def load_config() -> dict[str, Any]:
    """Load config from disk, falling back to defaults."""
    cfg = dict(DEFAULT_CONFIG)
    try:
        if _CONFIG_PATH.exists():
            with open(_CONFIG_PATH, "r", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                disk = json.load(fh)
            cfg.update(disk)
    except Exception:
        pass
    return cfg


def save_config(cfg: dict[str, Any]) -> None:
    """Persist config to disk."""
    with open(_CONFIG_PATH, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        json.dump(cfg, fh, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Flask app
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def create_app() -> Flask:
    # Suppress Flask's default request logging (every GET/POST pollutes stderr)
    import logging as _flog
    _flog.getLogger("werkzeug").setLevel(_flog.ERROR)

    app = Flask(__name__, static_folder=str(_DIR))

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # /chat — serve the chat UI
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    @app.route("/chat")
    def chat_ui():
        return send_from_directory(str(_DIR), "chat_ui.html")

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # /api/chat — proxy to DeepSeek / Kimi
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    @app.route("/api/chat", methods=["POST"])
    def api_chat():
        cfg = load_config()
        payload = request.get_json(force=True)

        messages: list[dict[str, Any]] = payload.get("messages", [])
        tools_supplied: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = payload.get("tools")
        tool_choice: str | None = payload.get("tool_choice")

        # Prepend system prompt if not already present
        if not any(m.get("role") == "system" for m in messages):
            messages.insert(0, {"role": "system", "content": cfg["system_prompt"]})

        provider = cfg["provider"]

        if provider == "deepseek":
            api_key = cfg.get("deepseek_api_key", "")
            base_url = cfg.get("deepseek_base_url", "https://api.deepseek.com")
            model = cfg.get("model", "deepseek-chat")
        elif provider == "kimi":
            api_key = cfg.get("kimi_api_key", "")
            base_url = cfg.get("kimi_base_url", "https://api.moonshot.cn/v1")
            model = cfg.get("model", "moonshot-v1-auto")
        else:
            return jsonify({"error": f"Unknown provider: {provider}"}), 400

        if not api_key:
            return jsonify({
                "error": (
                    f"No API key configured for {provider}. "
                    f"Set {provider}_api_key in config.json or use "
                    f"the /api/config endpoint."
                )
            }), 400

        # Build the request body (OpenAI-compatible format)
        body: dict[str, Any] = {
            "model": model,
            "messages": messages,
        }

        # Use provided tools or default Fusion tools
        if tools_supplied is not None:
            body["tools"] = tools_supplied
        else:
            body["tools"] = FUSION_TOOLS

        if tool_choice:
            body["tool_choice"] = tool_choice

        headers = {
            "Authorization": f"Bearer {api_key}",
            "Content-Type": "application/json",
        }

        endpoint = f"{base_url.rstrip('/')}/chat/completions"

        try:
            resp = requests.post(
                endpoint,
                json=body,
                headers=headers,
                timeout=120,
            )
            resp.raise_for_status()
            return jsonify(resp.json())
        except requests.exceptions.Timeout:
            return jsonify({"error": "AI provider request timed out (120s)."}), 504
        except requests.exceptions.HTTPError as exc:
            detail = ""
            try:
                detail = exc.response.text[:1000]
            except Exception:
                pass
            return jsonify({
                "error": f"AI provider returned {exc.response.status_code}: {detail}",
            }), 502
        except requests.exceptions.ConnectionError:
            return jsonify({"error": f"Cannot connect to {endpoint}"}), 502

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # /api/models — list available models
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    @app.route("/api/models")
    def api_models():
        cfg = load_config()
        return jsonify({
            "current_provider": cfg["provider"],
            "current_model": cfg["model"],
            "providers": {
                "deepseek": {
                    "models": ["deepseek-v4-flash", "deepseek-v4-pro"],
                    "base_url": cfg.get("deepseek_base_url", "https://api.deepseek.com"),
                    "configured": bool(cfg.get("deepseek_api_key")),
                },
                "kimi": {
                    "models": [
                        "moonshot-v1-auto",
                        "moonshot-v1-8k",
                        "moonshot-v1-32k",
                        "moonshot-v1-128k",
                    ],
                    "base_url": cfg.get("kimi_base_url", "https://api.moonshot.cn/v1"),
                    "configured": bool(cfg.get("kimi_api_key")),
                },
            },
        })

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # /api/config — read / update configuration
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    @app.route("/api/config", methods=["GET", "POST"])
    def api_config():
        if request.method == "GET":
            cfg = load_config()
            # Never return API keys in full
            safe = dict(cfg)
            safe["deepseek_api_key"] = (
                "***" + cfg["deepseek_api_key"][-4:]
                if len(cfg.get("deepseek_api_key", "")) > 4
                else ""
            )
            safe["kimi_api_key"] = (
                "***" + cfg["kimi_api_key"][-4:]
                if len(cfg.get("kimi_api_key", "")) > 4
                else ""
            )
            return jsonify(safe)

        # POST — merge updates
        cfg = load_config()
        updates = request.get_json(force=True)
        allowed_keys = {
            "provider", "model",
            "deepseek_api_key", "deepseek_base_url",
            "kimi_api_key", "kimi_base_url",
            "system_prompt",
        }
        for k, v in updates.items():
            if k in allowed_keys:
                cfg[k] = v
        save_config(cfg)
        return jsonify({"status": "ok", "updated": list(updates.keys())})

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # CORS — allow ONLY Fusion palette (Qt WebView on localhost) to connect
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    _LOCAL_ORIGINS = frozenset({
        "http://127.0.0.1:8765",
        f"http://127.0.0.1:{_DEFAULT_PORT}",
        "null",  # Qt WebEngine may send origin: null
    })

    @app.after_request
    def add_cors_headers(resp):
        origin = request.headers.get("Origin", "")
        if origin in _LOCAL_ORIGINS or not origin:
            resp.headers["Access-Control-Allow-Origin"] = origin or "http://127.0.0.1:8765"
        resp.headers["Access-Control-Allow-Headers"] = "Content-Type, Authorization, X-AIFusion-Token"
        resp.headers["Access-Control-Allow-Methods"] = "GET, POST, OPTIONS"
        return resp

    return app


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Thread-based launcher (used by AdamFusion.py when running in-process)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def start_in_thread(port: int | None = None) -> "threading.Thread":
    """Create and start the Flask app in a **daemon thread**.

    This avoids subprocess issues (wrong Python executable, missing
    dependencies in a child process).  The caller is responsible for
    ensuring ``flask`` and ``requests`` are importable beforehand.

    Returns the started :class:`threading.Thread` so the caller can
    check ``is_alive()`` or join on shutdown.
    """
    import threading as _threading

    port = port or int(os.environ.get("AIFUSION_PORT", _DEFAULT_PORT))

    # Ensure config.json exists
    if not _CONFIG_PATH.exists():
        save_config(DEFAULT_CONFIG)

    _app = create_app()

    def _run() -> None:
        try:
            _app.run(
                host="127.0.0.1",
                port=port,
                debug=False,
                use_reloader=False,
            )
        except Exception as exc:
            print(f"[aifusion] Flask thread error: {exc}")

    t = _threading.Thread(target=_run, daemon=True, name="AIFusionServer")
    t.start()
    return t


def wait_until_ready(host: str = "127.0.0.1", port: int = _DEFAULT_PORT,
                     timeout: float = 6.0) -> bool:
    """Poll ``/api/models`` and return ``True`` once the server responds.

    Blocks up to *timeout* seconds.
    """
    import time as _time
    import urllib.request as _request

    deadline = _time.monotonic() + timeout
    while _time.monotonic() < deadline:
        try:
            req = _request.Request(f"http://{host}:{port}/api/models", method="GET")
            _request.urlopen(req, timeout=1)
            return True
        except Exception:
            _time.sleep(0.2)
    return False


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Entry point
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def main() -> None:
    port = int(os.environ.get("AIFUSION_PORT", _DEFAULT_PORT))

    # Ensure config.json exists with defaults
    if not _CONFIG_PATH.exists():
        save_config(DEFAULT_CONFIG)
        print(f"[aifusion] Created default config at {_CONFIG_PATH}")
        print("[aifusion] Edit config.json to add your API key, then restart.")

    app = create_app()

    print(f"[aifusion] Local chat server starting on http://127.0.0.1:{port}")
    print(f"[aifusion] Chat UI:  http://127.0.0.1:{port}/chat")
    print(f"[aifusion] API:      http://127.0.0.1:{port}/api/chat")
    print(f"[aifusion] Config:   http://127.0.0.1:{port}/api/config")
    print("[aifusion] Press Ctrl+C to stop.")

    try:
        app.run(host="127.0.0.1", port=port, debug=False)
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        print("\n[aifusion] Server stopped.")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
